How to evaluate the semester break?
"How should the students evaluate the semester holiday?" asked the training expert-student coach Murat Aydın.
Graduation should not only be considered for the students; rest, entertainment, television, and time at the front of a computer and should not be considered.
Graduation is a very important opportunity to prepare for the new education period and to review the past period.
Mid-sea holiday, called leisure, is also an important opportunity for personality development, knowledge, skills and hobbies.
Make a mid-term evaluation list.
Write and try to apply everything that you're going to do, what you're going to plan.
I assure you, you will enjoy it and you will have a very productive semester.
Now let's first talk about what an efficient semester period for student friends who are preparing YGS-LYS.
"How should we evaluate this period, do we need to solve a lot of questions, or do we have missing issues?"
In order both to respond to them and to have a productive period, let's first enter our article with recommendations to the friends who are preparing for the exam.
The preliminary process should be a process that starts from the ninth grade under normal conditions, but we are trying to complete it in the last 1 year, which complies us to spend the last year more effective, efficient and more accurately using the last year.
In addition to exam preparation, the senior student also has to carry out the school's written work together.
It is also of critical importance for the year when the graduate will be preparing for the exam as a re-examination as a re-examination as a graduate student, even if the graduate has taken the exam (YGS-LYS) at least 1 time.
Because most alumni students and their loved ones consider 'O' year as last luck, which creates a greater stress.
To study is the work that the student doesn't get pleasure, he only does it because he doesn't feel compliant, and that's why he's always left it at the very end, but for the students who do it regularly, it's become an entirely task, and it's always within a plan of what's going to be done.
We've got a semester vacation ahead of us, and we need to make the most of it.
To do that, we must have a plan that will enable us to manage time well.
Course Working on a Mid-Year Holiday:
First of all, everyone needs to make a plan that suits their own situation.
The 1st term has been taken care of, what is missing; the day, the week and the 15-day time should be planned.
During this period, there should also be repetitions and question solutions.
At the same time, students who do not lack too much can also solve an average of 1-2 trial exams.
Excertain Your Missing Topics: Research shows that 75 per cent of what people have learned in a week, 66 per cent in a day, and 54 per cent within an hour.
The best and most influential way of eliminating acquittal is repetition.
Participants who have made a lot of mistakes from past issues should focus on their general studies again.
Determine your incomplete issues first and plan day by day, place the subject for every day and take care of them.
This planning will comfort you both academically and psychologically.
Be careful that when you place the topics on your plan, there are the things you're making the most mistakes.
'Cause you won't have such a prolonged holiday period later.
Make Question Solutions:
It's very important to solve a questionnaire.
'Cause we can only see how we understand the work we're doing, but we can see the feedback we get through the question we've solved.
Don't forget to put a specific number of question solutions every day.
The number of queries you will Sold may vary according to the studies you will do on that day; you may not be able to solve a lot of questions on a day you are working on, but we should at least see how much we have learned about the topic of that day.
Resolve Trial Exams:
Another part-of-a-half-time study should be to solve trial exams.
Even though the subjects are not all over, you can at least make course trial exam solutions.
Let's just say that you have largely taken the Turkish language course and you can solve trials for 40 questions.
And make sure you spend time while you're at it.
If you are able to solve the 40 Turkish question in 60 minutes at the same time your next goal will be to be able to be solved in a few less minutes.
Holiday And Hodja Plan:
Of course, it's not just about studying; you have to spend a few days for your holidays, relaxation and hobbies.
A holiday period that will only be spent by studying will prevent you from evacuating and resting.
That's why there should also be a special time for yourself within your plans.
Reading books, watching TV, surfing on the Internet can be in your plans, most importantly, how much time you're going to spend.
It'll also be a little piece of advice to friends who say we didn't spend the first term productive.
Well, my first term didn't go very well, I couldn't work very hard, and if you're saying a lot of deficiencies, it's a great opportunity for you.
But first of all, you have to decide and you have to believe it.
During the 2009-2010 Superleague, the most goals were scored between the 76th and 90th minutes.
Now you'll come back to the question you've been asking, the game's over, and you're going to the locker room, the game's still going, and there's a lot of minutes to score?
I don't think anybody would want to say, "We're going to look at the upcoming games," which is a classic comment used by a defeated football team teacher or players.
All you have to do right now has to leave the past and look in front of you, not to walk.
If we're gonna get what we're saying:
1) Preliminary one semester holiday plan,
2) Re-exason by going through the topics you know,
3) Resolve your missing issues,
4) Do issue consolidations by solving questions,
5) Resolve trial tests,
6) Read the book,
7) Determine new goals for the new period,
8) Make time for yourself, your hobbies and the things you enjoy,
9) Make time for your family and friends,
10) Make time for social and cultural activities (recitation, sports, theater, concerts, excursions, picnic, etc.)
