Xi wants to open the economy more to the world
President Xi Jinping told a group tasked with managing the reforms on Tuesday that the economy should be opened further to accelerate growth.
"Chinese should develop the policies of opening by attracting foreign investment expertise," he said at the 16th-Corporated Group meeting for Strengthening General Reforms.
While encouraging the opening, making new reforms will create a new space for economic growth by bringing a new energy and vitality, Xi said.
The leading group adopted a series of proposals such as a negative list regulating market access, relaxing border control policies, encouraging government-familiating institutions (SOE) to incorporate private equity, and a review of the registrar's registration system.
According to the statement, a negative list defining the restricted sector and business branches will be prepared for investment.
The system will be gradually tested and developed with trial programs.
It's an important move because it's going to play a greater role in alligating resources to the market, and it's going to make the market more clear by encouraging a law-based business environment.
At the same time, the government will loosen their control over the companies, enabling companies to carry out their own businesses.
China will also examine new cross-border economic co-operation models in the border regions and new mechanisms will come into force to promote regional growth.
In order to open government-controlled sectors, more space will be opened for private investment.
"Government will do not change its policy for foreign investment, and it will provide better services by preserving the interests of foreign-funded companies," the statement said.
In addition, foreigners will be optimized by optimising the necessities for permanent settlement permits or "green cards" and the application process will be facilitated.
Completion of the right to practiable lawmakers and educating professional judges and proceigans were also discussed at the meeting at the meeting.
Prime Minister Li Keqiang and senior leaders Liu Yunshan and Zhang Gaoli also attended the meeting according to a statement issued after the meeting.
